I have a Capacitor Android app. The app's WebView respects the Android system "Font size" accessibility setting, which causes text inside contenteditable elements to render at a scaled size that breaks CSS background-line alignment.

Fix: in MainActivity.java, override onCreate to lock the WebView text zoom to 100% so the system font size setting has no effect inside the app.

Find MainActivity.java (it will be under android/app/src/main/java/<package>/MainActivity.java). It likely currently extends BridgeActivity with an empty body. Add an onCreate override that calls super.onCreate(savedInstanceState) first, then this.bridge.getWebView().getSettings().setTextZoom(100). Add any required imports (android.os.Bundle). Do not change anything else.

